{"title":"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MadMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MadMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the greatest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that the cubic polynomial<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/6/336d7410dcc942dcdbcd1cc6edd104677a0cd18c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^{3} -\\frac{n}{6}x^{2} + (n - 11)x - 400\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"32\" />has roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/9/6c920c810f646e99b2e0e62a6e4816c1a0642376.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f6e7ff3e957b8dc764a99bc29f78882170fe820.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/b/17b2f19d3b84a0646d8ff157b73a03f37b99d1a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> are complex numbers, and there are exactly seven different possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/0/6a035ffa3d84fe213f219aa2701eec56985b63c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that positive/negative values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> give eight distinct values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/81923e07cdf5c93de485b9355e56b6641591fbcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />, so we conclude that for a choice of the three variables, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/7/b0767d608ae84911f779d128e4960bcb36a5fab8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />. (Testing other cases yields too few possible values.)\n</p><p>This is due to the fact that if we take either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/0/1f03534a4415725670716640ebe03fd2fed3a3bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/2/d32fbcbf1ab49803c9df6b12dd0b93a82f349485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\alpha,-\\beta,-\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />, both sums are equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>By Vieta, we get that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/9/4b9ba655224e74dfd3243e9a7a693e191bf5c7a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n-11=\\alpha^2\\beta^2+\\beta^2\\gamma^2+\\gamma^2\\alpha^2=(\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha)^2-2\\alpha\\beta\\gamma(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)=(\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha)^2\\]\" width=\"619\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/6106a73f50f33583dbb408df1ca974d356336c90.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n}{6}=\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2=(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)^2-2(\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha)=-2(\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha)=\\implies \\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha=-\\frac{n}{12}\\]\" width=\"735\" height=\"32\" />\nSubstituting, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/4365ecc88087b26161a8ebf66793a795120215a2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n-11=\\left(-\\frac{n}{12}\\right)^2=\\frac{1}{144}n^2\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"37\" />\nSolving the quadratic gives positive integer solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/808c723c6967a029f0fada8bdca5773bb986f50c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=12,\\boxed{132}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"102\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Eevee9406\">eevee9406</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We continue with the first solution with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/f/81fcd847dee9bb718f051b8755634804dcbbaa44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" />. Then,\nlet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> be the polynomial with roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> be the polynomial in the problem.\nThen,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/5/6a5eca29e1db179166ce4b54b361c7ce3de2cba0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(x) = (x-\\alpha) (x-\\beta) (x-\\gamma)\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/9/6491401cab067d87d6cffac2fd3983fc7f6a6579.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(-x) = -(x + \\alpha)(x + \\beta)(x + \\gamma).\\]\" width=\"268\" height=\"18\" />\nFrom Vieta's, there exists complex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afa3788b8437f5f02277dde509142e1c659d87be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = x^3 + px + q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"21\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2574175c3d2086b937334b9154be2da86c4dd5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-P(x)P(-x) = Q(x^2)\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/618290a2f2cc1d54c1c5e625996506da1c70f7a6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-(x^3 + px + q)(-x^3 - px + q) = x^6 - \\frac{n}{6} x^4 + (n-11)x^2 - 400,\\]\" width=\"492\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cfd8c4dad56fdf8d05377fa3399740453088f51.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^6 + 2px^4 + p^2x^2 - q^2 = x^6 - \\frac{n}{6} x^4 + (n-11)x^2 - 400.\\]\" width=\"426\" height=\"32\" />\nComparing coefficients, we need \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/a/58a62e469b8ba2106a5314363ec489e440571f63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p = \\frac{n}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f752168db1b281201fa0a7a05def3b2dc247120c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 = n-11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/cefb228f8a931fc4130dedbacbe69e4ed30d71b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/17531b756bc19a5c07c7f1ab8ce1cddf4bb4097c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$132$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, but we need the bigger one, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d5a3a58f30d2d11be50efb334d46189bbee00cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{132}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>made by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Binariouslyrandom\">BinariouslyRandom</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MadMath\">Video Solution by MadMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MadMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/44-b6STqF0s\">https://youtu.be/44-b6STqF0s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II\" title=\"2026 AIME II\">2026 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2026 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2026\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2026 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017213537\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 280/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1475/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7819/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.641      1 Template:AIME_box\n100.00%    7.641      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35495:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017213537 and revision id 284778. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}